feat(connections): Slice 1 — GitHub via PAT (connect -> token -> per-agent tool -> agent uses it live)

Atlas CONNECTIONS-ARCH. GitHub-first: no OAuth loopback, no verification —
the fastest end-to-end proof of the whole connection->token->per-agent-tool shape.

- db.rs migration 6: connection (keychain-backed credential + NON-secret
  metadata; key_ref is a POINTER, never the token) + agent_connection
  (per-agent enablement; the connection is the unit).
- connections.rs: keychain token slots (conn:<key_ref>:<slot>, namespaced);
  connect_github_pat (validate GET /user, capture login+scopes, store token,
  upsert row); provider_enabled_for_agent gate; token_for_agent_provider
  (reads keychain at call time); github_list_prs tool (open PRs via search API,
  token attached RUST-SIDE — jailed brain never holds the token); set/enabled/
  list/disconnect (disconnect wipes keychain slots).
- lib.rs: agent_tools_for_full threads (db, agent_id) so github_list_prs is
  surfaced ONLY when GitHub is connected+enabled for that agent; exec wired in
  all three provider paths (Anthropic/OpenAI/local); AGENT_SYSTEM unchanged.
  Cmds: github_connect, connections_list, connection_disconnect,
  connection_set_agent_enabled, connection_enabled_for_agent.
- UI: Connections tab enabled; Connections.tsx catalog card for GitHub
  (deep-link to token page + masked paste + validate + Connected as @login),
  per-agent enable checkbox, disconnect; Google Calendar card shown as
  "coming soon (pending OAuth verification)".

First compile of connections.rs + the tool-assembler refactor — flag if cargo throws.
